  "title": "LEGO Makes 36 Billion Bricks. You Get 4.5",
  "name_card": "What if LEGO split its bricks",
  "name_sub": "one year of bricks, shared out",
  "description": "What if LEGO shared one year of bricks with every person on Earth? Wikipedia says LEGO's annual brick production averages about 36 billion (an undated average, not a 2025 figure). Our math: Earth has more than 8 billion people (Wikipedia: the UN estimated 8 billion was passed on November 15, 2022). 36 billion / 8 billion = about 4.5 bricks each. The LEGO Eiffel Tower set (10307, 2022) has 10,001 parts (Wikipedia). 10,001 / 4.5 = about 2,220 years of your yearly share to build it. This is simple made-up math for fun, not a LEGO claim.\n\nSources:\n- Wikipedia: Lego: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lego\n- Wikipedia: World population: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_population\n\n#shorts #lego #whatif #howtheymakemoney",
